<p>When printing documents that contain high resolution bitmap images, 
 printing takes longer due to the larger amount of data that must be processed. 
 By changing the method for bitmap rendering, you can specify whether to 
 give priority to quality or speed .</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Priority:</span> 
 list, select an image processing priority.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2>Changing the Image Data Processing Method</h2>
<p>Depending on the application, there may be cases where printing takes 
 a long time, or colors are not reproduced correctly. In this kind of situation, 
 changing the image data processing method may rectify the problem.<br/>
Since changing the image data processing method may cause printing not 
 to function correctly with some applications, you should normally leave 
 this option unselected. </p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced 
 </span>menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Change Data Processing</span> 
 check box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
